WEBVTT

04:05.078 --> 04:09.122
What the hell?
Goddamn son-of-a-bitch...

04:24.138 --> 04:25.138
What the hell?

05:19.736 --> 05:21.611
Hey, my turn.

05:30.330 --> 05:33.999
Hey, what's wrong with this picture?

05:41.883 --> 05:44.009
Nice night for a walk?

05:48.723 --> 05:50.057
Nice night for a walk.

05:51.142 --> 05:55.395
Wash day tomorrow.
Nothing clean, right?

05:55.563 --> 05:57.105
Nothing clean. Right.

05:57.273 --> 06:00.317
I think this guy's a couple of cans
short of a six-pack.

06:00.485 --> 06:05.155
Your clothes, give them to me. Now.

06:05.323 --> 06:06.823
Fuck you, asshole.

07:50.553 --> 07:54.556
Hey, buddy, did you just see
a real bright light?

07:57.310 --> 07:58.685
See that guy?

07:58.853 --> 07:59.936
Hold it right there.

08:00.104 --> 08:01.938
- He's rabbiting.
- Hey! I said hold it!

08:02.106 --> 08:03.273
Go!

08:04.817 --> 08:07.777
That son-of-a-bitch took my pants.

08:51.656 --> 08:54.658
- What day is it? The date.
- 12th May.

08:54.825 --> 08:56.618
- Thursday.
- What year?

09:10.466 --> 09:12.133
He's got my gun. Let's go.

12:07.393 --> 12:09.728
Guard it for me, Big Buns.

12:13.190 --> 12:15.191
Hi. I'm late.

12:16.152 --> 12:17.777
So am I.

13:00.988 --> 13:03.281
- I'm in it.
- So am I.

13:09.121 --> 13:11.998
- Honey, can I have that coffee now?
- Yes, sir.

13:13.083 --> 13:15.543
- OK. Who gets the burly-beef?
- I ordered barbecued.

13:15.711 --> 13:17.754
I think that's mine,
but I didn't order fries.

13:17.922 --> 13:20.632
- Mine's the chili beef deluxe.
- OK, who gets the burly-beef?

13:20.800 --> 13:23.635
- Miss, we're ready to order now.
- Yes, ma'am.

13:25.888 --> 13:27.639
I'm so sorry.

13:30.810 --> 13:32.685
This isn't real leather, is it?

13:35.981 --> 13:39.150
Nice going, kid.
I ought to give you the tip.

13:41.445 --> 13:44.322
Look at it this way.
In 100 years, who's gonna care?

13:52.706 --> 13:54.874
The 12-gauge auto-loader.

13:57.002 --> 14:00.880
That's Italian. You can go pump or auto.

14:01.841 --> 14:04.592
The.45 long slide with laser sighting.

14:04.760 --> 14:08.054
These are new. We just got them in.
That's a good gun.

14:08.764 --> 14:10.515
Just touch the trigger,
the beam comes on,

14:10.683 --> 14:12.517
and you put the red dot where
you want the bullet to go.

14:12.685 --> 14:14.185
You can't miss.

14:16.188 --> 14:20.191
- Anything else?
- Plasma rifle in the 40-watt range.

14:20.359 --> 14:21.985
Hey, just what you see, pal.

14:23.279 --> 14:24.529
The Uzi nine millimeter.

14:26.073 --> 14:28.324
You know your weapons, buddy.

14:28.492 --> 14:30.660
Any one of these
is ideal for home defense.

14:31.871 --> 14:34.873
So which will it be?

14:35.040 --> 14:38.543
- All.
- I may close early today.

14:38.711 --> 14:43.047
It's a 15-day wait on the handguns,
but the rifles you can take now.

14:44.216 --> 14:46.217
- You can't do that.
- Wrong.

15:13.287 --> 15:16.039
Hi, baby. Yeah, yeah, it's me.

15:16.206 --> 15:20.501
Listen, I need you to come pick me up.
My bike just broke down.

15:20.669 --> 15:22.921
I don't care what you're doing.
Come and get me. What the?

15:24.548 --> 15:28.718
Hey, man, you got
a serious attitude problem.

16:21.814 --> 16:24.148
- Sarah Connor?
- Yes?

16:36.787 --> 16:39.205
I'm on my break, Chuck.
Carla's got my station.

16:39.373 --> 16:42.750
Sarah, come here. It's about you.
I mean, sort of.

16:45.295 --> 16:50.550
So incredible. You're not gonna believe
this. Sit, you're going to love this.

16:50.718 --> 16:53.845
- What?
...compiled from several witnesses.

16:54.013 --> 16:57.181
Once again, Sarah Connor,
35, mother of two,

16:57.349 --> 16:59.684
brutally shot to death
in her home this afternoon.

16:59.852 --> 17:01.644
You're dead, honey.

20:15.047 --> 20:17.048
...if you're into sound,

20:17.216 --> 20:21.552
for the greatest sound around,
come to Bob's Stereo at 2500 Sepulveda.

20:21.720 --> 20:25.932
We've got woofers, tweeters,
the newest in audio and compact discs.

20:26.099 --> 20:28.601
We've got graphic equalizers
and sound balancers that...

20:52.960 --> 20:54.418
Sorry.

21:06.598 --> 21:08.266
Hello?

21:08.433 --> 21:12.478
First I'm gonna rip the buttons
off your blouse one by one,

21:12.646 --> 21:17.066
then run my tongue down your neck
to your bare, gleaming breasts.

21:17.234 --> 21:22.947
And then slowly... slowly pull
your jeans off inch by inch.

21:24.324 --> 21:25.866
Ginger, it's Matt.

21:26.034 --> 21:29.954
And lick your belly in circles
further and further down,

21:30.122 --> 21:33.374
and then pull your panties off
with my teeth.

21:33.542 --> 21:34.834
Who is this?

21:36.461 --> 21:38.421
God. Sarah?

21:39.965 --> 21:42.216
Jesus. I'm sorry.

21:42.384 --> 21:45.177
I thought you were...
Can I talk to Ginger, please?

21:45.929 --> 21:46.929
Sure.

21:49.558 --> 21:51.142
It's the creep.

21:52.811 --> 21:53.811
Hello?

21:53.979 --> 21:57.523
First I'll rip the buttons off
your blouse one by one...

21:59.443 --> 22:04.447
You fucking pigs! Wait till I get
my hands on you. Get off me!

22:06.450 --> 22:07.700
Ed.

22:09.995 --> 22:12.038
- What have you got?
- Dead girl.

22:12.205 --> 22:15.708
- I can see that.
- Sarah Ann Connor, secretary, 35.

22:15.876 --> 22:19.712
Shot six times at less than ten feet.
Large caliber weapon.

22:19.880 --> 22:21.672
You know, these work.

22:23.050 --> 22:25.718
- What's this?
- Dead girl two.

22:25.886 --> 22:28.554
Sent over from the Valley division
this afternoon.

22:30.307 --> 22:32.808
Are you sure there's
a point to all of this?

22:32.976 --> 22:34.977
Look at the name, Ed.

22:35.729 --> 22:39.315
Sarah Louise Connor. Is this right?

22:41.026 --> 22:42.193
You're kidding me.

22:42.361 --> 22:44.945
The press is gonna be short-stroking it.

22:45.113 --> 22:49.450
- A one-day pattern killer.
- I hate the weird ones.

22:54.081 --> 22:55.915
So...

22:57.376 --> 22:59.710
Better than mortal man deserves.

23:07.010 --> 23:11.347
- Ginger, have you seen Pugsley?
- Not lately. Did you check messages?

23:11.515 --> 23:13.349
I thought you did.

23:18.188 --> 23:21.982
- Hi, Sarah, this is your mom...
- There you are, young man.

23:22.150 --> 23:24.318
You mind your mother.

23:28.448 --> 23:32.076
Hi, Sarah. Stan Morsky.
Something's come up.

23:32.244 --> 23:35.496
Looks like I won't be able to make it
tonight. Just can't get out of it.

23:35.664 --> 23:40.418
I'm really sorry. I'll make it up
to you. Call you in a day or so. Bye.

23:42.170 --> 23:45.589
That bum. So what if he has a Porsche?

23:45.757 --> 23:49.218
He can't treat you like this.
It's Friday night, for Christ's sake.

23:50.303 --> 23:52.304
I'll live.

23:52.472 --> 23:54.557
I'll break his kneecaps.

23:55.267 --> 23:59.645
Well, Pugsley still loves me.
Don't you, baby?

24:00.564 --> 24:02.857
God. It's disgusting.

24:05.110 --> 24:07.653
I'm gonna go to a movie, kiddo.
Have a good time.

24:07.821 --> 24:10.739
- We will. You, too.
- OK.

24:14.786 --> 24:16.912
Damn it, Matt.

25:13.678 --> 25:16.430
- Oh, shit.
- Lieutenant!

25:16.598 --> 25:20.100
These killings occurred in the order
of their listings in the phone book.

25:20.268 --> 25:23.187
- What can I tell you? No comment.
- But, Lieutenant...

25:35.659 --> 25:37.743
That coffee's two hours cold.

25:38.995 --> 25:40.913
I put a cigarette out in it.

25:42.082 --> 25:45.417
- Did you reach the next girl yet?
- No. I got her answering machine.

25:45.585 --> 25:47.878
- Send a unit.
- I sent a unit. There's no answer.

25:48.046 --> 25:50.214
- The apartment manager's not in.
- Call her.

25:50.382 --> 25:52.591
- I just called her.
- Call her again.

25:53.718 --> 25:55.302
Give me a cigarette.

26:05.564 --> 26:10.276
Hi, there. Fooled you.
You're talking to a machine.

26:10.443 --> 26:15.114
But don't be shy. It's OK. Machines need
love, too, so talk to it...

26:20.453 --> 26:21.912
Same shit.

26:23.248 --> 26:27.334
I can hear it now. He's gonna be
called the goddamn Phone Book Killer.

26:27.502 --> 26:32.756
I hate these press cases.
Especially the weird press cases.

26:34.259 --> 26:36.719
- Where are you going?
- To make a statement.

26:36.886 --> 26:39.054
Maybe make these jackals work for us
for a change.

26:39.222 --> 26:43.767
If I can get on the tube by 11:00,
maybe she'll call us.

26:43.935 --> 26:46.520
Well, how do I look?

26:46.688 --> 26:49.982
- Like shit, boss.
- Your mama.

26:51.109 --> 26:54.278
This just in. Police have announced
the name of the victim

26:54.446 --> 26:58.490
in the second of two execution
style murders which took place today.

26:58.658 --> 27:02.453
Incredibly, the names of the
two victims are virtually identical.

27:02.621 --> 27:07.166
Two hours ago, 35-year-old Sarah Ann
Connor was pronounced dead...

27:07.917 --> 27:10.127
- Can we change this?
- Sarah Louise Connor...

27:10.295 --> 27:11.879
Don't touch it!

27:13.965 --> 27:18.510
Police are refusing to speculate on the
similarity between the shooting deaths

27:18.678 --> 27:22.765
and no other connection between the
two victims has been established yet.

27:22.932 --> 27:26.310
We'll have more on this
late-breaking story as it comes in.

28:57.485 --> 28:59.737
- Hey, you got a phone?
- It's in the back.

28:59.904 --> 29:02.197
Hey, $4.50.

29:41.613 --> 29:44.656
You have reached the Los Angeles
Police Department emergency number.

29:44.824 --> 29:49.620
All lines are busy. If you need a police
car sent out to you, stay on the line.

30:53.893 --> 30:55.269
Pugsley! Shoo!

30:55.436 --> 30:58.063
Go on. I'm gonna make a belt out of you.

31:12.871 --> 31:14.705
Don't make me bust you up, man.

32:15.600 --> 32:19.061
Hi, there. Fooled you.
You're talking to a machine.

32:19.228 --> 32:22.105
But don't be shy. It's OK.
Machines need love, too.

32:22.273 --> 32:26.234
So talk to it and Ginger, that's me,
or Sarah will get back to you.

32:26.402 --> 32:27.903
Wait for the beep.

32:29.364 --> 32:31.365
Ginger, this is Sarah.
Pick up if you're there.

32:31.532 --> 32:37.371
I'm at this place on Pico Boulevard
called Tech Noir. I'm really scared.

32:37.538 --> 32:42.459
I think that there's somebody after me.
I hope that you play this back soon.

32:42.627 --> 32:45.754
I need you and Matt to come
and pick me up as soon as possible.

32:46.506 --> 32:49.633
The police keep transferring me around.
I'm gonna give 'em another try.

32:49.801 --> 32:54.054
The number here is 555-9175.

32:54.222 --> 32:56.139
Call me, kiddo. I need your help.

33:13.282 --> 33:14.574
It's her.

33:15.910 --> 33:18.078
Sarah Connor? It's Lieutenant Traxler.

33:18.246 --> 33:21.498
Lieutenant, don't put me on hold and
don't transfer me to another department.

33:21.666 --> 33:24.167
Don't worry, I won't. Just relax.
Can you tell me where you are?

33:24.335 --> 33:28.171
- I'm in this bar called Tech Noir.
- Yeah, I know it. It's on Pico.

33:28.339 --> 33:30.882
- Are you all right?
- Yeah, but I don't wanna leave.

33:31.050 --> 33:34.928
- I think there's a guy following me.
- Now, listen carefully.

33:35.096 --> 33:37.472
You're in a public place so
you'll be safe till we get there.

33:37.640 --> 33:39.933
But stay visible. Don't go outside
or even to the restroom.

33:40.101 --> 33:42.853
- I'll have a car there in a minute.
- OK.

34:07.128 --> 34:09.087
Hey, that guy didn't pay.

36:49.040 --> 36:50.790
Come with me if you wanna live.

36:59.926 --> 37:00.926
Come on!

38:14.208 --> 38:16.793
This is one-L-19.
I got a hit-and-run felony.

38:16.961 --> 38:21.298
Suspect vehicle: Late model
gray Ford headed westbound on Seventh.

38:21.465 --> 38:23.800
He's really moving,
punching lights all the way.

38:23.968 --> 38:27.762
I'm gonna need an ambulance
at Seventh and Broadway right now.

38:29.098 --> 38:30.140
Hold it!

38:47.283 --> 38:48.199
Hold on.

39:00.171 --> 39:03.840
Are you injured? Are you shot?

39:09.388 --> 39:12.766
Do exactly what I say. Exactly.

39:12.933 --> 39:16.478
Don't move unless I say.
Don't make a sound unless I say.

39:16.645 --> 39:18.063
Do you understand?

39:18.981 --> 39:22.609
- Do you understand?
- Yes! Please don't hurt me.

39:40.795 --> 39:42.545
I'm here to help you.

39:42.713 --> 39:47.300
I'm Reese. Sergeant Tech-Com.
DN38416. Assigned to protect you.

39:47.468 --> 39:49.177
You've been targeted for termination.

39:59.355 --> 40:03.733
This is one-L-19. Westbound
on Olympic, approaching Overland.

40:08.406 --> 40:11.866
This is a mistake. I didn't do anything.

40:12.034 --> 40:15.745
No, but you will.
It's very important that you live.

40:15.913 --> 40:19.290
This isn't true. How could that man
just get up after you...

40:19.458 --> 40:21.835
It's not a man. A machine.

40:22.002 --> 40:25.964
A Terminator.
Cyberdyne Systems model 101.

40:34.098 --> 40:38.059
A machine? Like a robot?

40:38.227 --> 40:42.730
Not a robot. A cyborg.
Cybernetic organism.

40:42.898 --> 40:45.817
- No. He was bleeding.
- Just a second.

40:49.196 --> 40:50.238
Get your head down!

41:35.201 --> 41:36.284
All right, listen.

41:36.452 --> 41:40.830
The Terminator's an infiltration unit.
Part man, part machine.

41:40.998 --> 41:45.084
Underneath it's a hyper-alloy combat
chassis. Microprocessor controlled.

41:45.252 --> 41:49.881
Fully armored, very tough.
But outside it's living human tissue.

41:50.049 --> 41:54.135
Flesh, skin, hair, blood...
grown for the cyborgs.

41:54.303 --> 41:56.846
- Look, Reese, I don't know...
- Pay attention.

41:57.014 --> 41:58.306
I gotta ditch this car.

42:03.938 --> 42:08.107
The 600-Series had rubber skin.
We spotted them easy.

42:08.275 --> 42:10.735
But these are new. They look human.

42:10.903 --> 42:14.531
Sweat, bad breath, everything.
Very hard to spot.

42:14.698 --> 42:18.409
I had to wait till he moved on you
before I could zero him.

42:18.577 --> 42:24.040
Look, I am not stupid.
They cannot make things like that yet.

42:24.208 --> 42:28.253
Not yet. Not for about 40 years.

42:30.881 --> 42:32.799
Are you saying it's from the future?

42:32.967 --> 42:35.051
One possible future.

42:36.053 --> 42:39.347
From your point of view,
I don't know tech stuff.

42:40.516 --> 42:42.725
Then you're from the future, too.
Is that right?

42:42.893 --> 42:45.019
- Right.
- Right.

42:53.279 --> 42:58.575
Cyborgs don't feel pain.
I do. Don't do that again.

42:58.742 --> 43:02.579
- Just let me go.
- Listen and understand.

43:02.746 --> 43:06.499
That Terminator is out there.

43:06.667 --> 43:10.336
It can't be bargained with,
it can't be reasoned with.

43:11.005 --> 43:15.216
It doesn't feel pity or remorse or fear

43:15.384 --> 43:21.264
and it absolutely will not stop,
ever, until you are dead.

43:31.442 --> 43:33.318
Can you stop it?

43:37.573 --> 43:38.906
I don't know.

43:40.784 --> 43:43.036
With these weapons, I don't know.

43:59.553 --> 44:03.848
All units. Ford suspect vehicle has
been found in a parking structure...

44:47.476 --> 44:51.771
Reese, why me?

44:53.857 --> 44:55.400
Why does it want me?

45:02.074 --> 45:04.200
There was a nuclear war.

45:06.370 --> 45:08.996
A few years from now...

45:10.708 --> 45:15.461
...all this, this whole place,
everything...

45:16.338 --> 45:20.967
...it's gone. Just gone.

45:22.010 --> 45:23.720
There were survivors.

45:23.887 --> 45:26.889
Here, there.

45:28.684 --> 45:31.144
Nobody even knew who started it.

45:33.814 --> 45:38.568
- It was the machines, Sarah.
- I don't understand.

45:38.736 --> 45:41.863
Defense network computers.

45:42.030 --> 45:45.199
New, powerful...

45:46.702 --> 45:50.621
...hooked into everything,
trusted to run it all.

45:51.415 --> 45:55.835
They say it got smart...
a new order of intelligence.

45:57.588 --> 46:00.757
Then it saw all people as a threat.
Not just the ones on the other side.

46:02.760 --> 46:05.553
It decided our fate in a microsecond.

46:07.222 --> 46:08.973
Extermination.

46:23.363 --> 46:24.864
Did you see this war?

46:37.294 --> 46:42.089
No. I grew up after. In the ruins.

46:42.257 --> 46:45.301
Starving. Hiding from the H-Ks.

46:45.469 --> 46:48.471
- H-Ks?
- Hunter-killers.

46:48.639 --> 46:52.391
Patrol machines
built in automated factories.

46:52.559 --> 46:56.813
Most of us were rounded up,
put in camps for orderly disposal.

46:58.857 --> 47:01.150
This was burned in by laser scanner.

47:05.113 --> 47:09.659
Some of us were kept alive. To work.

47:10.619 --> 47:11.994
Loading bodies.

47:13.121 --> 47:15.832
The disposal units ran night and day.

47:15.999 --> 47:18.876
We were that close
to going out forever.

47:21.964 --> 47:25.842
But there was one man
who taught us to fight.

47:26.009 --> 47:27.927
To storm the wire of the camps.

47:28.095 --> 47:31.389
To smash those metal
motherfuckers into junk.

47:33.016 --> 47:35.768
He turned it around.
He brought us back from the brink.

47:35.936 --> 47:40.189
His name was Connor. John Connor.

47:40.357 --> 47:44.819
Your son, Sarah. Your unborn son.

49:34.596 --> 49:35.596
Drive!

49:42.896 --> 49:45.982
Reese!

50:04.001 --> 50:07.378
No, Reese. No, no, no. They'll kill you.

50:07.546 --> 50:10.381
You in the Cadillac,
let me see your hands now.

50:13.552 --> 50:14.552
Get out of the car.

50:18.306 --> 50:20.516
Drop to your knees.

50:20.684 --> 50:23.310
- Out of the car.
- Drop to the ground.

50:52.632 --> 50:56.552
Sarah. Sarah, try to drink some of this.

50:59.556 --> 51:01.724
Listen, are you sure it's them?

51:01.892 --> 51:04.685
I mean,
maybe I should look at the bodies.

51:04.853 --> 51:07.730
No. They've been identified
and there's no doubt.

51:11.568 --> 51:13.444
Ginger.

51:15.030 --> 51:18.491
- Kiddo.
- Sarah...

51:18.658 --> 51:21.827
- Sarah, this is Dr. Silberman.
- Hi, Sarah.

51:21.995 --> 51:26.040
I want you to tell him everything
Reese told you. Do you feel up to that?

51:26.208 --> 51:28.292
Yeah, I guess so.

51:30.087 --> 51:33.923
- You're a doctor?
- Criminal psychologist.

51:34.091 --> 51:38.302
- Is Reese crazy?
- That's what we're gonna find out.

53:03.513 --> 53:07.016
So you're a soldier. Fighting for whom?

53:08.518 --> 53:13.564
With the 132nd under Perry.
From '21 to '27.

53:14.357 --> 53:16.817
That's the year 2027?

53:16.985 --> 53:19.069
That's right. Then I was assigned...

53:19.237 --> 53:22.865
- This is fucking great.
...under John Connor.

53:23.033 --> 53:26.118
- Who was the enemy?
- A computer defense system built...

53:26.286 --> 53:28.829
Goddamn. Sorry.

53:28.997 --> 53:32.333
...built for SAC-NORAD
by Cyberdyne Systems.

53:32.500 --> 53:34.460
I see.

53:34.628 --> 53:40.507
And this computer thinks it can win
by killing the mother of its enemy.

53:40.675 --> 53:43.886
Killing him, in effect,
before he's even conceived.

53:44.054 --> 53:46.138
A sort of retroactive abortion?

53:47.933 --> 53:51.185
Silberman cracks me up.
Last week, a guy burned his Afghan.

53:51.353 --> 53:53.854
- He screwed it first...
- Ed, shut up.

53:54.022 --> 53:56.357
Why didn't the computer
just kill Connor then?

53:56.524 --> 53:59.068
Why this elaborate scheme
with the Terminator?

53:59.236 --> 54:03.322
It had no choice.
Their defense grid was smashed.

54:03.490 --> 54:07.910
We'd won. Taking out Connor then
would make no difference.

54:08.078 --> 54:10.871
Skynet had to wipe out
his entire existence.

54:11.039 --> 54:16.085
Is that when you captured the lab
complex and found... What is it called?

54:16.253 --> 54:18.420
The time displacement equipment?

54:18.588 --> 54:22.633
That's right. The Terminator
had already gone through.

54:22.801 --> 54:25.678
Connor sent me to intercept
and they blew the whole place.

54:25.845 --> 54:27.680
Well, how are you supposed to get back?

54:28.556 --> 54:30.266
I can't.

54:31.768 --> 54:37.356
Nobody goes home.
Nobody else comes through.

54:38.108 --> 56:28.467
It's just him and me.

56:31.554 --> 56:36.517
Why didn't you bring any weapons?
Something more advanced.

56:36.684 --> 56:39.645
Don't you have ray guns?

56:39.813 --> 56:43.482
- Ray guns.
- Show me a piece of future technology.

56:43.650 --> 56:48.028
You go naked. Something about the
field generated by a living organism.

56:48.196 --> 56:50.239
- Nothing dead will go.
- Why?

56:50.407 --> 56:52.074
I didn't build the fucking thing.

56:52.242 --> 56:56.995
OK, OK. But this cyborg,
if it's metal?

56:57.163 --> 56:59.581
- Surrounded by living tissue.
- Oh, right.

57:00.375 --> 57:03.127
This is great stuff.
I could make a career out of this guy.

57:03.294 --> 57:06.088
See how clever it is?
It doesn't require a shred of proof.

57:06.256 --> 57:09.716
Most paranoid delusions are intricate,
but this is brilliant.

57:12.053 --> 57:16.014
- Why were the other two women killed?
- Most records were lost in the war.

57:16.182 --> 57:18.767
Skynet knew almost nothing
about Connor's mother.

57:18.935 --> 57:22.354
Her full name, where she lived.
They just knew the city.

57:22.522 --> 57:25.607
The Terminator was
just being systematic.

57:25.775 --> 57:28.610
- Let's go back...
- Look, you have heard enough.

57:28.778 --> 57:31.738
I have answered your questions,
now I have to see Sarah Connor.

57:31.906 --> 57:35.868
- I'm afraid that's not up to me.
- Then why am I talking to you?

57:36.035 --> 57:37.870
- Who is in authority here?
- Please...

57:38.037 --> 57:39.580
Shut up!

57:40.331 --> 57:42.958
You still don't get it, do you?

57:43.126 --> 57:48.213
He'll find her. That's what he does.
That's all he does.

57:48.381 --> 57:50.132
You can't stop him.

57:50.300 --> 57:53.927
He'll reach down her throat
and pull her fucking heart out!

57:54.095 --> 57:57.055
- Doc.
- Let go of me!

58:00.518 --> 58:01.518
Sorry.

58:06.941 --> 58:08.317
So Reese is crazy?

58:08.485 --> 58:11.987
In technical terminology, he's a loon.

58:12.822 --> 58:18.285
Sarah, this is what they call
body armor. Our TAC guys wear these.

58:18.453 --> 58:20.579
It'll stop a 12-gauge round.

58:20.747 --> 58:22.956
This other individual must've
been wearing one under his coat.

58:23.124 --> 58:24.791
Feel that. Go ahead.

58:27.086 --> 58:30.672
- He punched through the windshield.
- He was probably on PCP.

58:30.840 --> 58:33.509
Broke every bone in his hand.
He wouldn't feel it for hours.

58:33.676 --> 58:35.260
There was this guy once...
You see this scar?

58:35.428 --> 58:36.845
- Here.
- Thank you.

58:38.264 --> 58:42.017
There's a couch in this other room.
Stretch out and get some sleep.

58:42.185 --> 58:44.520
Be at least an hour before
your mother gets here from Big Bear.

58:44.687 --> 58:47.773
- I can't sleep.
- Try.

58:47.941 --> 58:52.194
It may not look it,
but that couch is very comfortable.

58:53.488 --> 58:57.991
You'll be perfectly safe.
We got 30 cops in this building.

58:58.868 --> 59:00.118
Thank you.

59:06.584 --> 59:08.418
- Good night.
- Good night.

59:23.268 --> 59:26.895
I'm a friend of Sarah Connor.
I was told she's here. Could I see her?

59:27.063 --> 59:29.231
No. Can't see her.
She's making a statement.

59:29.399 --> 59:30.524
Where is she?

59:31.484 --> 59:34.278
It may take a while. If you wanna wait,
there's a bench over there.

59:45.832 --> 59:47.332
I'll be back.

01:00:35.798 --> 01:00:38.342
- Are they terrorists?
- Let's go, let's go!

01:00:43.014 --> 01:00:44.389
Stay here.

01:00:58.613 --> 01:01:00.155
Let's get outta here!

01:01:24.597 --> 01:01:25.722
Watch him.

01:02:33.583 --> 01:02:34.916
Ed...

01:02:35.793 --> 01:02:37.127
Hey!

01:03:03.821 --> 01:03:05.280
Sarah!

01:03:06.616 --> 01:03:07.949
Reese.

01:03:11.871 --> 01:03:13.038
This way.

01:03:53.830 --> 01:03:56.498
KFLB news time 4:36.

01:03:56.666 --> 01:04:00.377
Top story of the hour: The largest
single law enforcement mobilization

01:04:00.545 --> 01:04:03.129
in California history
is currently underway.

01:04:03.297 --> 01:04:06.883
Police in five counties are engaged
in a massive manhunt for...

01:04:10.471 --> 01:04:11.847
Take this.

01:04:14.934 --> 01:04:16.643
All right,
let's get this off the road.

01:04:48.634 --> 01:04:51.511
- You cold?
- Freezing.

01:05:05.484 --> 01:05:06.651
Reese?

01:05:08.571 --> 01:05:12.282
- You got a first name?
- Kyle.

01:05:12.450 --> 01:05:16.745
Kyle, what's it like
when you go through time?

01:05:19.582 --> 01:05:21.416
White light.

01:05:23.878 --> 01:05:25.211
Pain.

01:05:28.507 --> 01:05:32.761
- It's like being born maybe.
- Oh, my God.

01:05:33.679 --> 01:05:35.597
I caught one back there.

01:05:37.183 --> 01:05:39.935
- You mean you got shot?
- It's not bad.

01:05:40.811 --> 01:05:44.272
- We gotta get you to a doctor.
- It's OK. Forget it.

01:05:44.440 --> 01:05:49.110
What do you mean, forget it?
Are you crazy? Take this off.

01:06:01.374 --> 01:06:03.375
Jesus.

01:06:03.542 --> 01:06:06.419
See? It passed right through the meat.

01:06:06.587 --> 01:06:08.213
This is gonna make me puke.

01:06:08.965 --> 01:06:11.758
- Would you just talk about something?
- What?

01:06:11.926 --> 01:06:15.387
I don't know. Anything.
Just talk. Tell me about my son.

01:06:17.223 --> 01:06:18.807
He's about my height.

01:06:22.478 --> 01:06:24.479
He has your eyes.

01:06:27.817 --> 01:06:29.401
What's he like?

01:06:30.194 --> 01:06:33.863
You trust him. He's got a strength.

01:06:35.574 --> 01:06:37.450
I'd die for John Connor.

01:06:40.371 --> 01:06:43.999
Well, at least now I know
what to name him.

01:06:45.167 --> 01:06:49.921
Don't suppose you know who the father is
so I won't tell him to get lost?

01:06:50.089 --> 01:06:52.841
John never said much about him.

01:06:53.009 --> 01:06:55.510
- I know he dies before the war...
- Wait.

01:06:57.430 --> 01:06:59.222
I don't wanna know.

01:07:00.516 --> 01:07:03.226
So was it John that sent you here?

01:07:03.936 --> 01:07:05.478
I volunteered.

01:07:06.731 --> 01:07:10.525
- Why?
- It was a chance to meet the legend.

01:07:11.610 --> 01:07:18.450
Sarah Connor,
who taught her son to fight, organize,

01:07:18.617 --> 01:07:20.702
prepare from when he was a kid.

01:07:20.870 --> 01:07:22.912
When you were in hiding before the war.

01:07:27.043 --> 01:07:30.462
You're talking about things
I haven't done yet in the past tense.

01:07:30.629 --> 01:07:32.505
It's driving me crazy.

01:07:36.385 --> 01:07:39.137
Are you sure you have the right person?

01:07:39.305 --> 01:07:41.347
I'm sure.

01:07:41.515 --> 01:07:45.226
Come on. Do I look like
the mother of the future?

01:07:47.063 --> 01:07:51.900
I mean, am I tough? Organized?
I can't even balance my checkbook.

01:07:54.695 --> 01:07:58.823
Look, Reese, I didn't ask
for this honor and I don't want it.

01:07:58.991 --> 01:08:00.450
Any of it.

01:08:03.746 --> 01:08:07.957
Your son gave me a message
to give to you. Made me memorize it.

01:08:09.293 --> 01:08:12.003
"Thank you, Sarah,
for your courage through the dark years.

01:08:12.171 --> 01:08:14.297
I can't help you with
what you must soon face,

01:08:14.465 --> 01:08:16.758
except to say the future is not set.

01:08:16.926 --> 01:08:19.427
You must be stronger than
you imagine you can be.

01:08:19.595 --> 01:08:22.097
You must survive or I will never exist."

01:08:23.432 --> 01:08:24.891
That's all.

01:08:27.853 --> 01:08:29.395
It's a good field dressing.

01:08:30.940 --> 01:08:32.440
You like it?

01:08:33.192 --> 01:08:34.609
It's my first.

01:08:38.906 --> 01:08:41.282
Get some sleep. It'll be light soon.

01:08:45.538 --> 01:08:46.788
OK.

01:08:57.466 --> 01:08:59.384
Talk to me some more.

01:09:02.638 --> 01:09:04.180
About what?

01:09:05.391 --> 01:09:07.517
Tell me about where you're from.

01:09:09.979 --> 01:09:11.479
All right.

01:09:13.399 --> 01:09:17.902
You stay down by day,
but at night you can move around.

01:09:18.070 --> 01:09:21.990
You still have to be careful
because the H-Ks use infrared.

01:09:24.118 --> 01:09:29.164
But they're not too bright.
John taught us ways to dust them.

01:09:30.624 --> 01:09:32.876
That's when the infiltrators
started to appear.

01:09:33.043 --> 01:09:35.086
The Terminators were the newest.

01:09:35.713 --> 01:09:36.629
The worst.

01:09:46.682 --> 01:09:51.269
Traversing your sector in search mode.
750 meters north of your position.

01:09:56.233 --> 01:09:57.358
Let's go.

01:10:42.821 --> 01:10:46.783
- Reese. DN384...
- Right. Let him in.

01:12:18.292 --> 01:12:20.168
Terminator!

01:13:37.413 --> 01:13:39.747
I was dreaming about dogs.

01:13:40.999 --> 01:13:43.376
We use 'em to spot Terminators.

01:13:44.461 --> 01:13:47.004
Your world is pretty terrifying.

01:14:25.794 --> 01:14:29.714
Hey, buddy,
you got a dead cat in there or what?

01:14:37.055 --> 01:14:39.223
Fuck you, asshole.

01:14:58.076 --> 01:14:59.911
God damn.

01:15:00.996 --> 01:15:02.455
Thank you.

01:15:07.836 --> 01:15:09.337
Is this enough?

01:15:10.005 --> 01:15:13.174
Yeah, it's enough.
I don't wanna ask where you got it.

01:15:19.515 --> 01:15:21.015
- I'm coming.
- We need a room.

01:15:21.183 --> 01:15:23.184
- All right.
- With a kitchen.

01:15:23.352 --> 01:15:24.810
Do you have one with a kitchen?

01:15:40.869 --> 01:15:43.704
I am dying for a shower.

01:15:45.332 --> 01:15:47.500
We should check your bandage, too.

01:15:48.085 --> 01:15:50.753
Later. I'm going out for supplies.

01:15:55.467 --> 01:15:56.634
Keep this.

01:16:22.703 --> 01:16:26.080
No, I can't tell you where I am, Mom.
I was told not to say.

01:16:26.248 --> 01:16:28.416
But I need to know where to reach you.

01:16:28.584 --> 01:16:33.713
You tell me to hide out at the cabin
and you won't tell me what's going on?

01:16:33.880 --> 01:16:36.632
I am worried sick here.

01:16:36.800 --> 01:16:40.553
OK. OK, here's the number.

01:16:40.721 --> 01:16:42.930
- You ready?
- Yes. Go ahead.

01:16:43.098 --> 01:16:49.770
It's 408-555-1439. Room nine.

01:16:49.938 --> 01:16:51.689
- Got it?
- I've got it.

01:16:51.857 --> 01:16:56.027
I gotta go. I'm sorry
I can't tell you more right now.

01:16:56.194 --> 01:16:57.945
I love you, Mom.

01:17:01.450 --> 01:17:03.326
I love you, too, sweetheart.

01:17:16.214 --> 01:17:18.633
- Tiki Motel.
- Give me your address there.

01:17:22.304 --> 01:17:23.387
What have we got?

01:17:27.100 --> 01:17:33.230
Mothballs... corn syrup... ammonia.

01:17:33.398 --> 01:17:35.024
What's for dinner?

01:17:35.734 --> 01:17:38.819
- Plastique.
- That sounds good.

01:17:38.987 --> 01:17:40.363
What is it?

01:17:41.281 --> 01:17:44.825
It's a nitroglycerin base.
It's a bit more stable.

01:17:44.993 --> 01:17:46.869
I learned to make it when I was a kid.

01:17:58.757 --> 01:18:00.883
Make sure there's none on the threads.

01:18:03.095 --> 01:18:04.512
Like this.

01:18:06.473 --> 01:18:08.265
Screw the end cap on.

01:18:10.185 --> 01:18:11.727
Very gently.

01:18:14.481 --> 01:18:16.774
You must've had a fun childhood.

01:18:20.487 --> 01:18:21.862
That's good.

01:18:22.823 --> 01:18:25.866
All right. Six more like that
and I'll get started on the fuses.

01:18:37.337 --> 01:18:39.296
He'll find us, won't he?

01:18:42.300 --> 01:18:43.801
Probably.

01:19:01.903 --> 01:19:04.029
It'll never be over, will it?

01:19:12.456 --> 01:19:14.457
Look at me. I'm shaking.

01:19:15.667 --> 01:19:20.755
Some legend.
You must be pretty disappointed.

01:19:21.840 --> 01:19:25.760
No, I'm not.

01:19:34.478 --> 01:19:39.774
Kyle, the women in your time,

01:19:39.941 --> 01:19:42.026
what are they like?

01:19:44.112 --> 01:19:46.197
Good fighters.

01:19:46.364 --> 01:19:48.407
That's not what I meant.

01:19:50.577 --> 01:19:52.411
Was there someone special?

01:19:54.456 --> 01:19:55.998
Someone?

01:19:56.625 --> 01:19:58.793
A girl, you know.

01:20:00.295 --> 01:20:01.670
No.

01:20:04.466 --> 01:20:06.091
Never.

01:20:07.677 --> 01:20:09.303
Never?

01:20:14.267 --> 01:20:17.645
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

01:20:20.524 --> 01:20:22.608
So much pain.

01:20:23.985 --> 01:20:28.322
Pain can be controlled.
You just disconnect it.

01:20:28.490 --> 01:20:30.741
So you feel nothing?

01:20:35.914 --> 01:20:38.833
John Connor gave me
a picture of you once.

01:20:40.752 --> 01:20:42.545
I didn't know why at the time.

01:20:44.005 --> 01:20:49.844
It was very old, torn, faded.

01:20:53.682 --> 01:20:59.687
You were young like you are now.
You seemed just a little sad.

01:21:01.231 --> 01:21:03.983
I used to always wonder
what you were thinking at that moment.

01:21:05.443 --> 01:21:07.653
I memorized every line...

01:21:09.155 --> 01:21:11.031
...every curve.

01:21:14.703 --> 01:21:16.620
I came across time for you, Sarah.

01:21:18.540 --> 01:21:22.835
I love you. I always have.

01:21:40.896 --> 01:21:42.563
I shouldn't have said that.

01:23:13.446 --> 01:23:14.655
Think fast.

01:24:44.704 --> 01:24:46.038
Trade places.

01:24:57.050 --> 01:25:00.385
Faster! Drive faster!

01:25:50.311 --> 01:25:53.480
Kyle! Oh, my God.

01:26:27.724 --> 01:26:29.057
Kyle.

01:26:44.324 --> 01:26:45.699
Son-of-a-bitch!

01:27:01.382 --> 01:27:02.382
You stay here.

01:27:26.366 --> 01:27:27.532
Let's get outta here.

01:27:31.204 --> 01:27:32.454
Get out.

01:27:49.597 --> 01:27:52.557
Kyle. Come on. Get up.

01:28:01.109 --> 01:28:03.652
Kyle, come on.

01:28:04.779 --> 01:28:07.656
Help me! Get out. Get out.

01:28:32.140 --> 01:28:34.099
Don't stop. Run!

01:30:46.274 --> 01:30:47.816
Sarah!

01:30:48.860 --> 01:30:50.485
Kyle.

01:30:55.783 --> 01:30:58.326
Kyle. Kyle...

01:31:00.413 --> 01:31:03.165
We did it, Kyle. We got him.

01:31:22.894 --> 01:31:25.812
No!

01:32:21.702 --> 01:32:22.994
Wait.

01:32:27.833 --> 01:32:29.459
What are you doing?

01:32:30.336 --> 01:32:33.505
Cover, so he can't track us.

01:32:43.224 --> 01:32:46.393
Come on! Come on.

01:32:46.561 --> 01:32:50.230
No, Kyle! Come on!

01:32:50.982 --> 01:32:52.732
- Come on!
- Leave me here.

01:33:03.869 --> 01:33:08.248
Move it, Reese! On your feet, soldier!

01:33:08.583 --> 01:33:10.750
On your feet!

01:33:11.377 --> 01:33:12.544
Move it!

01:34:24.241 --> 01:34:25.909
Get back. Go back.

01:35:00.444 --> 01:35:02.237
- Run, Sarah.
- No.

01:35:02.405 --> 01:35:09.119
Run!

01:35:09.704 --> 01:35:11.246
Come on, motherfucker.

01:37:04.235 --> 01:37:06.402
No.

01:39:04.897 --> 01:39:06.564
You're terminated, fucker.

01:40:04.748 --> 01:40:05.999
Kyle.

01:40:27.021 --> 01:40:31.024
Tape seven. November 10. Where was I?

01:40:31.984 --> 01:40:35.820
What's most difficult is trying to
decide what to tell you and what not to.

01:40:36.530 --> 01:40:40.533
But I guess I have a while before you're
old enough to understand these tapes.

01:40:40.701 --> 01:40:44.454
They're more for me at this point
just so that I can get it straight.

01:41:21.575 --> 01:41:22.909
Fill her up.

01:41:26.580 --> 01:41:29.707
Should I tell you about your father?

01:41:29.875 --> 01:41:32.126
Boy, that's a tough one.

01:41:33.670 --> 01:41:38.174
Will it affect your decision to send him
here, knowing that he is your father?

01:41:40.427 --> 01:41:43.179
If you don't send Kyle,
you can never be.

01:41:43.347 --> 01:41:46.432
God, a person could go crazy
thinking about this.

01:41:50.104 --> 01:41:51.979
I suppose I will tell you.

01:41:53.816 --> 01:41:55.608
I owe him that.

01:41:58.028 --> 01:42:00.363
Maybe it'll help if...

01:42:00.531 --> 01:42:05.952
...you know that in the few hours
that we had together...

01:42:07.621 --> 01:42:10.039
...we loved a lifetime's worth.

01:42:22.928 --> 01:42:26.764
- What did he just say?
- He says you're very beautiful.

01:42:26.932 --> 01:42:29.809
He is ashamed to ask you for five
American dollars for this picture.

01:42:29.977 --> 01:42:33.396
But if he doesn't,
his father will beat him.

01:42:33.564 --> 01:42:35.273
Pretty good hustle, kid.

01:42:52.624 --> 01:42:54.208
What did he just say?

01:42:54.960 --> 01:42:57.044
He said there's a storm coming in.

01:43:01.466 --> 01:43:03.050
I know.

01:47:10.215 --> 01:47:11.048
OCR by FHD
